    <notes>
      <html:body xmlns:html="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <html:p>Source: user-provided Seydoux2022_MxlPy.ipynb, based on Seydoux et al. 2022, DOI 10.1111/nph.18003.</html:p>
        <html:p>The MxlPy quasi-steady PSII 4x4 linear solve is represented by mathematically equivalent algebraic assignment rules B0-B3.</html:p>
        <html:p>The stored PPFD value is constant for simple timecourses; notebook Figures 3b/3c require a segmented PAM pulse schedule plus computation of NPQ from pulse maxima. NPQ is not a dynamic species.</html:p>
        <html:p>Reaction stoichiometries assume the original b_H=100 and HPR=14/3 values. If changing either parameter, re-export the SBML stoichiometry.</html:p>
      <html:p>NPQ is an auxiliary mathematical readout species (not a biological compound). No original ODE or reaction has been altered. The reporter derivative follows the chain rule exactly.</html:p><html:p>Preview: PPFD=200 begins from the WT state after 1000 s dark adaptation. Model output NPQ=(Fm_dark_virtual-Fm_sat_virtual(t))/Fm_sat_virtual(t), using a virtual instantaneous 5000 PPFD fluorescence probe.</html:p><html:p>IMPORTANT: This is an instantaneous NPQ proxy for live display, not an exact recreation of the 0.8 s pulse maxima from Seydoux notebook. The original published Figure 3b/3c reproduction still requires the PAM protocol and analysis script.</html:p></html:body>
    </notes>
